@page "/razor-syntax"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Razor Syntax</PageTitle>

<h1>Razor syntax</h1>

<p class="lead">
    A <code>.razor</code> file mixes HTML markup with C#. The <code>@@</code> character is the
    Razor transition: whatever follows it is treated as C# (or a directive), everything else is HTML.
</p>

<hr/>

<h2>1. Anatomy of a .razor file</h2>

<pre><code>@@page "/razor-syntax"          // route this page is reached at
@@rendermode InteractiveServer  // enables event handlers / binding

&lt;PageTitle&gt;Demo&lt;/PageTitle&gt;     // sets the browser tab title

&lt;h1&gt;Hello, world!&lt;/h1&gt;          // ordinary HTML, written as-is

&lt;p&gt;You are visitor @@number&lt;/p&gt; // @@number renders the field value

@@code {                        // C# members live here
    private int number = 42;
}</code></pre>

<ul>
    <li>Files <em>with</em> <code>@@page</code> are routable pages.</li>
    <li>Files <em>without</em> <code>@@page</code> are reusable components (e.g. <code>Compare.razor</code>).</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Directives</h2>

<table class="table">
    <thead>
    <tr>
        <th>Directive</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
    </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>@@page "/route"</code></td><td>Makes the file a routable page.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@code { ... }</code></td><td>C# members (fields, methods, event handlers).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@functions { ... }</code></td><td>Older alias for <code>@@code</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@using Namespace</code></td><td>Import a namespace (also global in <code>_Imports.razor</code>).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@inject IService svc</code></td><td>Dependency injection (equivalent to <code>[Inject]</code>).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@inherits BaseType</code></td><td>Inherit from a base class (e.g. <code>LayoutComponentBase</code>).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@implements IInterface</code></td><td>Implement an interface, e.g. <code>IDisposable</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@attribute [StreamRendering]</code></td><td>Apply a C# attribute to the component class.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@rendermode InteractiveServer</code></td><td>Runs this page in an interactive server circuit.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@layout MainLayout</code></td><td>Pick a layout for this page.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@typeparam TItem</code></td><td>Makes the component generic.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@namespace X.Y</code></td><td>Override the generated class namespace.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>@@preservewhitespace true</code></td><td>Keep whitespace in the rendered output.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Expressions</h2>

<p>An <code>@@</code> followed by a value is an <em>implicit</em> expression. Use parentheses for an
    <em>explicit</em> expression when Razor would otherwise misread the boundary.</p>

<pre><code>@@message                    // implicit: prints the field value
@@message.ToUpper()          // implicit: method call
@@(message)suffix            // explicit: @(message) then "suffix"
@@messagesuffix              // BAD: Razor reads "messagesuffix"</code></pre>

<div class="mb-3">
    <p>Implicit expression: <span class="fw-bold">@message</span></p>
    <p>Explicit expression: <span class="fw-bold">@(2 + 3)</span> (and fruit count is <span class="fw-bold">@fruits.Count</span>)</p>
    <p>Method call: <span class="fw-bold">@DateTime.Now.ToShortDateString()</span></p>
    <p>Parenthesised expression then literal text: <span class="fw-bold">@(message) suffix</span></p>
</div>

<h2>4. Control flow</h2>

<pre><code>@@if (condition) { ... } else { ... }

@@for (int i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) { ... }

@@foreach (var item in items) { ... }

@@switch (value) { case "a": ... break; default: ... break; }</code></pre>

<h5>@@if / @@else (live)</h5>
<button class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" @onclick="() => showExtra = !showExtra">
    @(showExtra ? "Hide" : "Show") extra paragraph
</button>
@if (showExtra)
{
    <p class="alert alert-info mt-2">This <code>@@if</code> block is rendering right now.</p>
}
else
{
    <p class="alert alert-light mt-2">Nothing extra (the <code>@@else</code> branch is active).</p>
}

<h5 class="mt-3">@@for (live)</h5>
<div>
    @for (var i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
    {
        <span class="badge text-bg-secondary me-1">@i</span>
    }
</div>

<h5 class="mt-3">@@foreach (live)</h5>
<ul>
    @foreach (var fruit in fruits)
    {
        <li>@fruit</li>
    }
</ul>

<h5 class="mt-3">@@switch (live)</h5>
<div class="mb-2">
    @foreach (var letter in new[] { "alpha", "beta", "gamma" })
    {
        <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary me-1" @onclick="() => kind = letter">@letter</button>
    }
</div>
@switch (kind)
{
    case "alpha":
        <p>You picked alpha.</p>
        break;
    case "beta":
        <p>You picked beta.</p>
        break;
    default:
        <p>Pick a letter above.</p>
        break;
}

<h2>5. Inline code blocks: <code>@@{ }</code></h2>

<p>Use <code>@@{ ... }</code> to run a few statements and define local variables inline (not persisted).</p>

<pre><code>@@{
    var greeting = "Hello";
    var now = DateTime.Now;
}
&lt;p&gt;@@greeting, the time is @@now.ToString("HH:mm").&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="mb-3">
    @{
        var greeting = "Hello";
        var now = DateTime.Now;
    }
    <p class="fw-bold">@greeting, the time is @now.ToString("HH:mm").</p>
</div>

<h2>6. Comments</h2>

<pre><code>@@* A Razor comment: stripped out, never sent to the browser. *&#64;

&lt;!-- An HTML comment: kept and sent to the browser. --&gt;

@@code {
    // C# line comment
    /* C# block comment */
}</code></pre>

<p>Right-click this page and choose <em>View Page Source</em>: the Razor comment is gone, the HTML comment is there.</p>

<h2>7. Writing literal text: <code>@@:</code> and <code>&lt;text&gt;</code></h2>

<p>Inside a code block (like <code>@@if</code>), Razor expects HTML. To emit raw text instead,
    start a line with <code>@@:</code> or wrap it in <code>&lt;text&gt;</code>.</p>

<pre><code>@@if (showText) {
    @@: A plain-text line.
    &lt;text&gt;Another raw text line.&lt;/text&gt;
}</code></pre>

<div class="mb-3">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" @onclick="() => showText = !showText">Toggle text</button>
    @if (showText)
    {
        @: A plain-text line written with @@:
        <text>Another raw text line written with &lt;text&gt;.</text>
    }
</div>

<h2>8. Attributes, events and data binding</h2>

<pre><code>&lt;button @@onclick="Increment"&gt;Click&lt;/button&gt;              // event handler method
&lt;button @@onclick="() =&gt; count++"&gt;Click&lt;/button&gt;         // event handler lambda
&lt;button @@onclick="Increment" @@onclick:stopPropagation&gt; // stop event bubbling
&lt;a @@onclick="Go" @@onclick:preventDefault href="#"&gt;Link&lt;/a&gt; // suppress default behavior

&lt;input @@bind="text" /&gt;                        // two-way binding (change event)
&lt;input @@bind="text" @@bind:event="oninput" /&gt;  // bind on every keystroke

&lt;p @@ref="paragraph"&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;                   // element reference
&lt;li @@key="item.Id"&gt;...&lt;/li&gt;                   // identity hint for list diffing
&lt;div @@attributes="extraAttrs"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;       // splat a dictionary of attrs</code></pre>

<div class="row g-3">
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <p>Count: <span class="fw-bold">@count</span></p>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="Increment">Increment (event method)</button>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <input class="form-control" @bind="boundText" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="Type something..."/>
        <p class="mt-2">You typed: <span class="fw-bold">@boundText</span></p>
    </div>
</div>

<h2>9. The <code>@@code</code> block</h2>

<pre><code>@@code {
    private int count = 0;                 // field used by markup above
    private string? boundText;

    private void Increment() =&gt; count++;   // method invoked by @@onclick

    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        // you can await async work here
    }
}</code></pre>

